# No `file:` package links

Never put `"file:..."` in `package.json` `dependencies`, `devDependencies`, or `peerDependencies`. That includes sibling ECP packages. `file:` breaks CI, GitHub Pages, and any install that does not share this machine’s directory layout.

Committed `@executioncontrolprotocol/*` deps use registry ranges (e.g. `^0.12.0`).

For local unpublished packages, use `npm link` after `npm run build` in the ECP monorepo. Do not substitute `file:` even temporarily in committed `package.json`.
